CORE
main.cpp
--cpp98
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ static member built by private ctor: SUCCESS$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
N5008 [class.access.general]/7 -- an out-of-class static data member
definition has MEMBER access and may call the class's private
constructor.  The front end used to judge the initializer from
namespace scope ("member 'S::S(this)' is not accessible"); fixed by
re-entering the member's class scope around the initializer's
type-checking.  Was the residual blocker for dog-fooding
src/goto-programs/goto_trace.cpp (trace_optionst::default_options).
Header-free, 12 essential lines.
